Assessment: This is the segment with the largest air-terminal demand by volume in Indonesia (dozens of mall/office/condo projects run concurrently each year by ~8 large listed developers), but purchasing decisions are highly fragmented — there is no centralized "state owner" as in infrastructure/hospitals; each project''s main contractor/MEP subcontractor chooses suppliers based on existing agency relationships. A favorable point for STARDUCT (AMCA-aligned, mid-market pricing): mid-tier projects from Summarecon/Ciputra/Alam Sutera (regional malls, Class B/B+ offices) are less brand-sensitive than premium projects like Thamrin Nine or Pakuwon/PIK2''s Class-A superblocks — where international brands (Johnson Controls, and brands that ride along with international MEP consultants like Meinhardt) are already entrenched. TKDN (local content) is NOT mandatory for private commercial real estate (only mandatory for government/BUMN projects) — not a legal barrier in this segment, though it warrants further confirmation against Kepmenperin regulations if a higher degree of certainty is required. Confidence note : specific MEP contractor names could not be identified for most projects (the sole exception being Thamrin Nine); precise land bank/GFA figures for Agung Podomoro, Sinar Mas Land, and Ciputra could not be identified; 2025-2026 data for Lippo Karawaci/Lippo Malls could not be found through public sources.
