2C. Which Brands Dominate Which Segments (medium confidence — inferred from regional patterns)
• Data centers : TROX, Halton, and American brands (via regional channels) are commonly specified for Tier III/IV projects due to strict pressure/airflow control requirements.
• Hospitals/cleanrooms : Halton and TROX have strong global positioning and likely dominate in HK, alongside Japanese brands (Daikin''s industrial line).
• Commercial office/malls : mixed — premium projects use international brands (TROX, Systemair), mid-tier projects use local fabricators or mainland Chinese products.
• Industrial/warehouse : dominated mainly by local fabricators and low-cost mainland Chinese products.
2D. Specification Practices & Key MEP Consultants
• Arup — a global firm with an HK office, involved in numerous major infrastructure projects.
• AECOM — active in MEP design in HK, has published work on "MiMEP" (Modular Integrated MEP).
• J. Roger Preston Limited (JRP) — headquartered in HK, flagship projects: the Data Centre at the Tamar Government Complex, China Unicom (HK) Global Center (Tseung Kwan O).
• Meinhardt (Hong Kong) Limited — established 1974, multi-project M&E consultancy in HK and the region; also involved in the structural design of Kai Tak Hospital.
• Key reference standard : the ArchSD (Architectural Services Department) "General Specification for Air-conditioning, Refrigeration, Ventilation and Central Monitoring & Control System Installation" — the standard spec document for public-works projects, which mandates ductwork mainly to HVCA DW/144 (British) , with SMACNA (American) used only where DW/144 does not apply; damper leakage testing to EN 1751, fire performance to BS 476; filters to ASHRAE 52.1 and EN-779/Eurovent. → HK is a hybrid British-American-EU market , leaning toward British/EN standards more than the ASEAN markets.
2E. MEP Contractors Purchasing Air Terminals (target customers)
MEP Contractor | Specialization | Source/Contact
