Observation: Systemair has made the largest committed investment and has the clearest local legal presence in KSA; TROX and Halton maintain a smaller sales-representative/branch-level presence.
2C. Brand Dominance by Segment (no quantitative data, inferred indirectly)
• Cleanroom/hospital/pharmaceutical : Halton (dedicated Jeddah office), alongside specialized cleanroom contractors (FTS Cleanrooms, ASPAR Engineering, Ziebaq) — a highly technical segment that typically specifies international brands with dedicated certifications.
• Data center/commercial towers/giga-projects : large projects designed by international consultants tend to specify global brands (TROX, Systemair, Krueger, Price) for high-spec items, but use local AMCA-certified manufacturers (SAFID, Sharqawi, Dania) for bulk volume to meet localization requirements — inferred from industry structure, not project-specific data.
• General commercial/residential construction : local AMCA-listed manufacturers dominate on price, lead time, and localization scoring.
