AECOM, Atkins (SNC-Lavalin), Cundall, Hilson Moran, Parsons | Appear in Middle East MEP consultant rankings, but the specific KSA vs UAE vs Qatar allocation is unverified
On reference standards : the KSA construction industry operates under the Saudi Building Code (SBC), whose mechanical section (SBC 501 - Mechanical) was developed in cooperation with the ICC, based on the US International Mechanical Code (IMC) — not the UK BS/EN system. For ductwork/air terminals, common industry practice across the GCC (including KSA) is to specify SMACNA (duct construction/fabrication) and AMCA (damper/louver/grille performance) — precisely the standards system STARDUCT already holds an advantage in. Some projects led by British consultants (Atkins, Cundall, Hilson Moran, Buro Happold) may blend in additional BS/EN standards for fire-related items (BS 476) — clearly seen in Sharqawi''s certification (BS476 Part 24) alongside UL. Conclusion: the ASHRAE/SMACNA/AMCA framework dominates, with a BS/EN overlay for fire protection — not a purely BS/EN system.
