2C. Degree of dominance by segment
• Data centers : top-tier projects (NTT, Viettel IDC, CMC, VNG) are typically built by large MEP contractors to international specs; the specific brands used are unverified, but regional trends suggest locally present brands (Kruger, TROX) are approved more easily due to lead time and technical support.
• Hospitals/cleanrooms : dominated by Japanese contractors (Takasago Vietnam, Shinryo) and cleanroom specialists (Vietnam Cleanroom, AAF Asia via Viet Phat); air terminals typically follow Japanese/US specs.
• Offices/commercial/malls : the largest segment by volume — domestic fabricators (STARDUCT, Dai Phuc, BKVN) hold the edge thanks to price and delivery speed; premium landmark projects (foreign investors, international consultants) may specify foreign brands.
• Industrial/FDI (Samsung, Foxconn, LG, etc.): domestic fabricators have a cost/JIT advantage, but some Korean/Japanese FDI plants tend to favor familiar brands when the general contractor is a Korean or Japanese firm.
